G4820.def:
συν-βάλλω
(Rec. συμ-), [in LXX: 2 Chroniques 25:19 (גָּרָה hith.), Ésaïe 46:6 (זוּל), Jérémie 43:3 (סוּת hi.), Wis.5:8, al. ;] 
to throw together, hence, 
__(a) of speech (before λόγους, Eur., al.), to discuss, confer (sc. λόγους): with dative of person(s), Luc 11:53, WH, mg., Actes 17:18; before πρὸς ἀλλήλους, Actes 4:15; 
__(b) to reflect, consider, ponder: ἐν τ. καρδίᾳ, Luc 2:19; 
__(with) to meet with, fall in with: Actes 20:14; in hostile sense, εἰς πόλεμον, with dative (εἰς μάχην, Polyb.), Luc 14:31; 
__(d) mid., to contribute (Polyb., al.; cf. MM, xxiv): Actes 18:27.†

G4864.def:
συν-αγωγή, -ῆς, ἡ 
[in LXX chiefly for עֵדָה, also for קָהָל, etc. ;] 
prop., a bringing together; 
__1. of things, 
__(a) a gathering in of harvest; 
__(b) a collection of money. 
__2. Of persons, 
__(a) a collecting, assembling (Polyb.); 
__(b) an assembly (MM, xxiv; Deiss., LAE, 101 ff.): Apocalypse 2:9 3:9; esp. of a Jewish religious assembly, a synagogue: Luc 12:11, Actes 9:2, al.; of a Christian assembly, Jacques 2:2. By meton., of the building in which the assembly is held, a synagogue: Matthieu 10:17, Marc 1:21, al. (cf. Cremer, see word ἐκκλησία) 
SYN.: ἐκκλησία (which see)
